                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "NOTE: These are just my initial impressions on the Early Access version. I've got high hopes for this game, regardless of the bad first impression. However, in its current state, I can't recommend it.\n\nThe story and intended gameplay, as far as I know what it's supposed to be, is awesome and very inventive. The game itself, as it is, is fairly unplayable. You start the game, have no instructions and the 'settings' menu doesn't work (perhaps it's not implemented yet). You have, a kind of, 3rd person view and when you look around certain points of interest on your screen might show up, but you don't have a cursor or pointer or anything of the sort to determine what location you're actually looking at. This also makes reacting in a hurry quite impossible. In my first play [spoiler]I switched view to one of the other characters and saw my original char slide over the floor, get dressed and rise up to his waist in the ceiling. He proceeded to float towards the main room in his default rigging pose, until I switched view to him. Once the emergency activated he 'switched' to run mode which consisted of him making a weird crouch and 'running' as if he had a pilates ball stuck between his legs, making him look as though he was in a hurry to find the nearest toilet.[/spoiler]\n\nThat being said, the game isn't expensive at all and I believe that, by the time its finished, these (and other) issues will be fixed and we are going to have one hell of an experience on our hands.",
